/**
@page view_model The view model

Every BONet operation acts on a *view*: a handle to one header within one
packet. A view is declared by the caller, initialized by the library, and passed
to the functions that read or modify that header.

@section view_model_opaque Opaque handle

A view is a small stack value. Declare one and pass its address to the library:

@code{.c}
bnt_eth  eth;
bnt_ipv4 ip;
@endcode

Parsing and navigation initialize it (see @ref parsing); the other functions
read it back. Its fields are private and may change between releases. Do not
access them directly.

@section view_model_const Const-correctness

Read accessors take a pointer to a @c const view. Functions that modify the
packet take a non-const view. The signature alone distinguishes the two:

@code{.c}
int bnt_ipv4__get_ttl(const bnt_ipv4 *ip, __u8 *out);   /* reads  */
int bnt_ipv4__set_ttl(bnt_ipv4 *ip, __u8 ttl);          /* writes */
@endcode
*/
